 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "Run it backwards",
   "text": "Take the Carnot loop and go round it **anticlockwise**: \\(a\\to d\\to c\\to b\\to a\\). Every stroke is reversible, so each one now does the opposite. The engine becomes a **refrigerator**: it needs work.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "ph": 0,
      "wk": 0
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 5500
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "a → d: adiabatic expansion",
   "text": "Insulated, the gas expands and **cools** from \\(T_1\\) to \\(T_2={{T2|0}}\\) K, colder than the cold box.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "wk": 0
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "ph": 0.995
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 3600
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 5200
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "d → c: isothermal expansion",
   "text": "On the cold reservoir the gas expands at \\(T_2\\) and **absorbs** heat \\(Q_2\\) from it. This is the useful stroke: the cold box is being cooled.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "wk": 0
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "ph": 1.995
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 3600
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 5200
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "c → b: adiabatic compression",
   "text": "Insulated again, the piston compresses the gas and it **warms** from \\(T_2\\) to \\(T_1={{T1|0}}\\) K, hotter than the room.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "wk": 0
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "ph": 2.995
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 3600
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 5200
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "title": "b → a: isothermal compression",
   "text": "On the hot reservoir the gas is compressed at \\(T_1\\) and **dumps** heat \\(Q_1\\) into it. Back at \\(a\\): one cycle done.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "wk": 0
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "ph": 3.995
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 3600
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 5200
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "title": "Energy balance",
   "text": "Over the cycle \\(\\Delta U=0\\). Heat in: \\(Q_2={{Q2|0}}\\) J. Heat out: \\(Q_1={{Q1|0}}\\) J. So the work **done on** the gas is \\(W=Q_1-Q_2={{Wn|0}}\\) J (the area of the loop, now an input).",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "ph": 4,
      "wk": 1
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 6000
  },
  {
   "id": "s6",
   "title": "Coefficient of performance",
   "text": "A fridge is judged by the heat it removes per joule of work: \\(\\text{CP}=\\dfrac{Q_2}{W}=\\dfrac{Q_2}{Q_1-Q_2}\\). With \\(Q_2/Q_1=T_2/T_1\\) this gives \\(\\text{CP}=\\dfrac{T_2}{T_1-T_2}={{cp|2}}\\). The smaller the temperature gap, the more heat per joule.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "ph": 4,
      "wk": 1
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 7000
  }
 ],
