   "title": "Coefficient of performance",
   "tex": "\\text{CP}=\\dfrac{Q_2}{W}=\\dfrac{T_2}{T_1-T_2}",
   "text": "For a reversed Carnot engine (an ideal refrigerator).",
   "filled": "\\text{CP}=\\dfrac{ {{T2|0}} }{ {{T1|0}}-{{T2|0}} } = {{cp|2}}"
  },
  {
   "title": "Energy balance",
   "tex": "W = Q_1 - Q_2",
   "text": "Work done on the gas, heat \\(Q_2\\) taken in at \\(T_2\\), heat \\(Q_1\\) rejected at \\(T_1\\)."
  }
 ],
 "challenges": [
  {
   "id": "c1",
   "type": "number",
   "title": "Now you try",
   "prompt": "An ideal refrigerator works between \\(T_2=300\\) K and \\(T_1=500\\) K. Find its coefficient of performance.",
   "answer": 1.5,
   "hint": "Use \\(T_2/(T_1-T_2)\\).",
   "explain": "\\(\\text{CP}=300/(500-300)=1.5\\).",
   "set": {
    "T1": 500,
    "T2": 300
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "c2",
   "type": "choice",
   "title": "Now you try",
   "prompt": "In a refrigerator, heat flows from cold to hot. Why is that allowed?",
   "options": [
    {
     "id": "a",
     "label": "It is not allowed"
    },
    {
     "id": "b",
     "label": "Because work is done on the gas"
    },
    {
     "id": "c",
     "label": "Because \\(\\Delta U\\) is positive"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "b",
   "hint": "Think of the second law wording: \"by itself\".",
   "explain": "Heat cannot flow cold → hot **by itself**. With work supplied by a motor it can."
  }
 ],
 "takeaways": [
  "Reverse the Carnot loop and it becomes a refrigerator: \\(W\\) in, \\(Q_2\\) from cold, \\(Q_1\\) to hot.",
  "\\(W=Q_1-Q_2\\) as before.",
  "\\(\\text{CP}=T_2/(T_1-T_2)\\)."
 ],
